/**
 * The `text-decoration-line` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property sets
 * the kind of decoration that is used on text in an element, such as an underline or overline.
 *
 * Initial: none. Inherited: no.
 * Percentages: not accepted.
 *
 * Keyword effects:
 * - blink: The text blinks (alternates between visible and invisible). Conforming user agents may
 * not blink the text. This value is deprecated in favor of [CSS
 * animations](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/animation).
 * - grammar-error: Each line of text uses the user agents' method of highlighting grammar mistakes,
 * which is a dotted green line in most browsers.
 * - line-through: Each line of text has a decorative line going through its middle.
 * - none: Produces no text decoration.
 * - overline: Each line of text has a decorative line above it.
 * - spelling-error: Each line of text uses the user agents' method of highlighting spelling
 * mistakes, which is a dotted red line in most browsers.
 * - underline: Each line of text has a decorative line beneath it.
 *
 * Grammar: none | [ underline || overline || line-through || blink ] | spelling-error |
 * grammar-error
 *
 * Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-text-decor-4/#propdef-text-decoration-line
 *
 * Author guide:
